[12¶36] ADDENDUM (Jo's question, Oct 28): « équipement » should cite Recherches 13 (CERFI, Dec 1973), « Généalogie du capital 1. Les équipements du pouvoir », not only the 1976 book; Querrien is a co-author, and Deleuze, Guattari, Foucault took part in its conversations. Row is append-only; swap in a corrected gloss by hand if wanted.
[12¶41] ADDENDUM (Jo's question, Oct 28): « plan » has a third sense here: the French national Plan (Commissariat général du Plan). Recherches 13 ch. V, « le Discours du Plan », analyzes the planning reports (Plan de Modernisation et d'Equipement, 1947, p. 200; the sixth Plan's équipements collectifs, p. 197; method, p. 195). The architect's « plan métrique sur papier » sits beside the State's Plan; Querrien (fns. 21, 24) writes out of this CERFI work. Gloss as a resonance, not as D&G's stated reference.
